message: "If you use AZRAS System, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "AZRAS System"
abstract: >-
  RESEARCH RECORD — UNFINISHED. DO NOT USE FOR DECISIONS. AZRAS System v2.2.0
  is published intentionally unfinished, as a research record of AI-assisted
  software development. A cross-audit found known inconsistencies in its
  calculation results (documented in README.md). Estimated construction costs
  and construction-method comparisons from this release must not be used for
  design, construction, investment or business decisions, and must not be
  cited as evidence of the cost or performance of any construction method.
  AZRAS System is an open-source desktop suite for planning, evaluating and
  comparing buildings over a 200-year life cycle. It reads construction
  drawings printed to PDF, performs quantity takeoff, and sends items it
  cannot resolve to several independent AI systems; each AI answer is kept as
  a separate candidate with its evidence, compared only between like
  quantities and units, and never adopted by majority vote. Unresolved items
  are routed to human review. The suite calculates CO2 emissions and energy
  use from 8,760-hour regional weather data, compares insulation
  specifications, construction methods and building locations, and evaluates
  200-year business cash flow and environmental load. The same drawing set can
  be resent to multiple AIs at later dates, with SHA-256 hashes preserving
  drawing identity, to observe longitudinal changes in AI drawing-reading
  capability. v2.2.0 comprises four products: Installer, Planning, Evaluation
  and Compare.
